                        "entry_id": "3ff9f7ca-c03c-31ec-877c-3dde42a91ea8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The rattlesnake Sistrurus catenatus (formerly Crotalinus catenatus) in the family Viperidae, found in three subspecies."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eeebbfbb-70d7-478c-97ad-6c10912d3d11",
                                "sense_id": "e4287165-086d-33cd-86fb-632c0ceeea3b",
                                "text": "I hope in this paper to contribute something to the knowledge of the Prairie Rattlesnake, or Massasauga (Caudisona tergemina)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6500427-ef5c-414f-bce7-a375f5f0020b",
                                "sense_id": "e4287165-086d-33cd-86fb-632c0ceeea3b",
                                "text": "The Massasauga is emphatically a species of the prairies and their swamps and marshes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d701632-2f13-4da1-8bc0-ae1a7f65b1b8",
                                "sense_id": "e4287165-086d-33cd-86fb-632c0ceeea3b",
                                "text": "According to the zoologist, the massasaugas were found abroad from mid-April to late October, chiefly during the daylight hours and for an average 197 days annually during the study period."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
